                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d4493b5-3e25-4a2e-9e07-cf3cb732f2db",
                        "source_entry_id": "66a69a0b-c9e6-3ebf-9db5-7d705093cda3",
                        "source_sense_id": "2d3b5d9a-7310-3d6b-9091-0d7226aa6fe3",
                        "source_sense_description": "weiblicher Vorname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Fanny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Fanny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89fa2d51-e395-34db-a2fb-c1c1bc3c05d6",
                                        "entry_id": "611bf85a-262f-39ee-ab2e-3d51f4604355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A diminutive of the female given name Frances, itself also becoming a given name."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "592d9d18-ed4c-4d18-8ed5-e953f62c85b0",
                                                "sense_id": "89fa2d51-e395-34db-a2fb-c1c1bc3c05d6",
                                                "text": "\"My name is Frances. Don't call me Fanny!\" \"Why not?\" \"Because it's too absurd to be endured! What does the mere sound of Fanny suggest? A flirting dancing creature - plump and fair, and playful and pretty!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a23cd9c-8245-4f88-bc5f-f19c20060d69",
                                                "sense_id": "89fa2d51-e395-34db-a2fb-c1c1bc3c05d6",
                                                "text": "They listened to the sound of Fanny’s retreating footsteps. ‘Well, well!’ said Marcus. ‘Oh, take no notice Jess. You know what our Frances Maud is like! It’s nothing to cry about!’ To her humiliation Jessamy found there were tears trickling down her cheeks. ‘Always getting worked up about something, Fanny is.’\n– page 105:\nAs she did so Fanny put down her book , stood up and stretched her arms, and at once Jessamy noticed a difference. It was the same Fanny but not the Fanny who climbed trees and tore her frock playing in the garden. It was as though a young lady film had settled over her, neatening her unruly hair, which was tied back with a large black bow, and primly composing her small mouth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b94afb6b-e3ed-4438-ab19-58873a1eeab8",
                                                "sense_id": "89fa2d51-e395-34db-a2fb-c1c1bc3c05d6",
                                                "text": "\"I spose you want to be a cattleboy,\" drawled the multicolored beard whose name was Carrol Day, a curiously feminine name, thought Martin, not yet acquaintanced with the bearded Marions, Fannys and Abbys of Texas who, saddled by their unthinking mothers with dainty names, built savagely masculine frames of character."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fcfaf001-6693-41f0-bc57-9e3aa6a4bbe6",
                        "source_entry_id": "66a69a0b-c9e6-3ebf-9db5-7d705093cda3",
                        "source_sense_id": "2d3b5d9a-7310-3d6b-9091-0d7226aa6fe3",
                        "source_sense_description": "weiblicher Vorname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Stephanie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Stephanie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a7f3159-4025-3dcf-9a54-0a1bf146a918",
                                        "entry_id": "46f3c4b5-fcf0-3d1c-8d32-f535e1190e82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from French."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca1c9dc2-acff-49de-8115-e46052577a95",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7f3159-4025-3dcf-9a54-0a1bf146a918",
                                                "text": "Allison made a careful note of the address and within the hour she had met, decided she liked, and moved in with a girl of twenty who called herself Steve Wallace.\n\"Don't call me Stephanie\", Steve had said. \"I don't know why it should, but being called Stephanie always makes me feel like something pale and dull out of Jane Austen.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb3b6f5a-2e2d-46aa-818b-430453221de2",
                                                "sense_id": "2a7f3159-4025-3dcf-9a54-0a1bf146a918",
                                                "text": "The sponsor of the Utah legislation, Republican Rep. Stephanie Gricius, acknowledged fluoride has benefits, but said it was an issue of “individual choice” to not have it in the water."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e52db36-19c9-4162-9445-3ab2643c548a",
                        "source_entry_id": "66a69a0b-c9e6-3ebf-9db5-7d705093cda3",
                        "source_sense_id": "2d3b5d9a-7310-3d6b-9091-0d7226aa6fe3",
                        "source_sense_description": "weiblicher Vorname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Stéphanie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Stéphanie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df5d33ea-fd05-358d-9dae-bdc16f3ff194",
                                        "entry_id": "129d9292-a8cf-3aee-911d-4b68021a1e4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prénom féminin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37138072-a655-42d5-8723-92b11c9dbdcf",
                                                "sense_id": "df5d33ea-fd05-358d-9dae-bdc16f3ff194",
                                                "text": "Immobile auprès d’elle, Geneviève tenait à la main un rameau que Stéphanie était sans doute allée détacher de la plus haute cime d’un peuplier, et l’idiote agitait doucement ce feuillage au-dessus de sa compagne endormie, pour chasser les mouches et fraîchir l’atmosphère."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ff5cd06-1f8a-412e-bc7e-46da6c2dcce0",
                                                "sense_id": "df5d33ea-fd05-358d-9dae-bdc16f3ff194",
                                                "text": "On n’est donc pas dans une rigueur budgétaire, constate Stéphanie Villers, économiste et conseillère économique à PwC France."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d5fe1b8-a84e-4229-bd96-93d7ce20fe0a",
                                                "sense_id": "df5d33ea-fd05-358d-9dae-bdc16f3ff194",
                                                "text": "Stéphanie Lafontaine propose, quant à elle, des animations destinées aux enfants, les mardis à 10 h et les jeudis, à 13 h 30, durant les vacances, et tous les samedis à 14 h, le reste de l’année."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
